"""Reviewed grade for every optimization tweak — generated by
_dev/import_tier_review.py, do not edit by hand.

Source review sheet : tweak_tier_review.csv
Imported            : 2026-10-02 23:18 UTC
Tweaks covered      : 515

This is the reviewed, human-signed-off grade for each optimization
tweak. :func:`database.classification.grade_optimization` returns these
values verbatim, so what ships is what was reviewed rather than a
re-derived heuristic guess.

``database.classification.classify_optimization`` is unchanged: it still
computes the heuristic grade from the implementation facts and is used
as the fallback for any tweak missing from this table (and for the
diagnostic / System Tools entries, which are not tier-reviewed). Keeping
the heuristic intact means the shipped grade stays auditable -- the
difference between the two is reviewable, not hidden.

Grades are the uppercase classification axis (FREE / FOUNDATION /
MAXIMUM) and are deliberately *not* plan names; the plan that unlocks a
tweak is derived from the grade via
``database.classification.PLAN_FOR_GRADE``.
"""
